# Copy this file to `.env.analytics.local` and fill in your dev Aptabase key.
#
# `.env.analytics.local` is gitignored (matched by the `*.local` pattern in
# .gitignore) so the key is never committed.
#
# The key is sourced by `scripts/dev-with-analytics.sh` and exported to the
# cargo build via APTABASE_APP_KEY, where it is baked into the binary by
# `option_env!` in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`.
#
# Use a DEDICATED "openehr-explorer-dev" Aptabase project so local clicks
# don't pollute production metrics — see ADR-0018.
#
# Get a key at https://aptabase.com after creating the dev project. It will
# look like:
#
#     A-EU-1234567890   (EU region, hosted)
#     A-US-1234567890   (US region, hosted)
#     A-DEV-1234567890  (local self-hosted Aptabase on localhost:3000)
#
# Usage:
#
#     cp .env.analytics.example .env.analytics.local
#     $EDITOR .env.analytics.local
#     npm run dev:analytics

APTABASE_APP_KEY=
